---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import GithubHeatmap from '../components/GithubHeatmap.astro';
import Clippy from '../components/Clippy.astro';
import PostList from '../components/PostList.astro';
import TagCloud from '../components/TagCloud.astro';
import risanPhoto from '../assets/risan.webp';
import { getPosts, groupByTerm } from '../lib/posts';

const posts = await getPosts();
const curiosityLetters = [...'curiosity'];
const featured = posts.filter((p) => p.data.featured).slice(0, 6);
const recent = posts.slice(0, 6);

const tags = groupByTerm(posts, 'tags');
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Risan Bagja"
  description="Tutorials and notes on web development, tooling, and the things I break along the way."
>
  <div class="home-intro">
    <h1>
      Code, <span class="curiosity-nowrap"><button
          id="curiosity-trigger"
          class="curiosity-trigger"
          type="button"
          aria-label="curiosity"
          aria-controls="clippy-widget"
          aria-expanded="false"
          title="Psst. Click me."
        >
          <span class="curiosity-flame" aria-hidden="true">{curiosityLetters.map((letter, index) => (
            <span class="curiosity-letter" style={`--i: ${index}`}>{letter}</span>
          ))}</span></button>,</span> and a questionable number of agents
    </h1>

    <div class="home-intro-spread">
      <p>
        Hi, I’m Risan. I build software for a living. It started in junior high, when I got bored with
        Flash games and picked up a book about Borland Delphi 6. I followed the tutorials and made a simple
        text editor. Then I wanted to make something else.
      </p>
      <p>
        I published some of my early software as RdF, short for &ldquo;Reason da Freak.&rdquo; It was
        supposed to sound like &ldquo;Risan the Freak.&rdquo; Don&rsquo;t judge me.
      </p>
      <p>
        Since then, I’ve built websites for clients, worked with startups on their products, and
        helped companies make sense of their data. I enjoy turning a rough idea into working software
        and sorting out all the details that never make it into the first conversation. I usually
        stay with a project through deployment and whatever happens once real people start using it.
      </p>
      <p>
        These days, building software feels less like sitting at an editor and more like running a very
        busy control room. AI agents research the problem, argue over the approach, write the code,
        test it, and review one another’s work. I designed the rules and checkpoints that keep the whole
        thing moving in the right direction. Most of the time, I watch it unfold, provide context when
        needed, and adjust the workflow based on what goes wrong. It’s a strange way to build software,
        and I’m having a lot of fun figuring it out.
      </p>

      <figure class="home-intro-figure">
        <Image
          src={risanPhoto}
          alt="Risan Bagja looking out the train window"
          class="home-intro-photo"
          loading="eager"
          fetchpriority="high"
          widths={[380, 520, 760, 1176]}
          sizes="(max-width: 768px) 100vw, 540px"
        />
        <figcaption class="home-intro-caption">I only go out when my Claude Code usage has drained out completely.</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <p>
        I’m usually tinkering with something on the side too: maps, small web apps, ESP32 boards,
        sensors, or whatever else has caught my attention. This site is where I write down what I learn,
        including the things that took longer to figure out than I’d like to admit. Hopefully, something
        here saves you an afternoon.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="home-columns">
    {
      featured.length > 0 && (
        <section class="section-block">
          <h2>Featured</h2>
          <PostList posts={featured} />
        </section>
      )
    }

    <section class="section-block">
      <h2>Recent</h2>
      <PostList posts={recent} />
      <p class="eyebrow" style="margin-top: 20px;">
        <a href="/posts/">All {posts.length} posts →</a>
      </p>

    </section>
  </div>

  <section class="section-block">
    <h2>Tag Cloud</h2>
    <TagCloud groups={tags} />
  </section>

  <GithubHeatmap />
  <Clippy />

<style>
  .home-intro-spread {
    margin-top: 28px;
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .home-intro-spread {
      columns: 2;
      column-gap: 52px;
      margin-top: 36px;
    }

    /* The columns stay balanced; a paragraph split across them keeps at least
       three lines on each side, as in print. */
    .home-intro-spread p {
      orphans: 3;
      widows: 3;
    }
  }

  .home-intro-spread p {
    margin: 20px 0 0;
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .home-intro-spread p:first-of-type {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .home-intro-spread p:first-of-type::first-letter {
    initial-letter: 2;
    -webkit-initial-letter: 2;
    float: left;
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 3.4rem;
    line-height: 0.85;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--accent);
    margin: 0.04em 0.14em 0 0;
  }

  .home-intro-figure {
    break-inside: avoid;
    margin: 24px 0;
  }

  .home-intro-photo {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    aspect-ratio: 16 / 10;
    object-fit: cover;
    object-position: center 63%;
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    border-radius: 4px;
    background: var(--sunk);
  }

  .home-intro-caption {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    text-align: center;
    margin-top: 10px;
    padding: 0 8px;
  }

  .curiosity-nowrap {
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .curiosity-trigger {
    --flame-ember: #9e2a10;
    --flame-heat: #d9501f;
    --flame-glow: #ec7a1e;
    --flame-core: #f4a321;
    --flame-halo: rgba(240, 110, 40, 0.35);

    appearance: none;
    padding: 0;
    border: 0;
    border-radius: 4px;
    background: none;
    color: var(--accent);
    font: inherit;
    letter-spacing: inherit;
    cursor: pointer;
    -webkit-tap-highlight-color: transparent;
    transition: transform 0.15s cubic-bezier(0.34, 1.56, 0.64, 1);
  }

  :global(html.dark) .curiosity-trigger {
    --flame-ember: #d0451f;
    --flame-heat: #f2703f;
    --flame-glow: #ffb547;
    --flame-core: #ffe39a;
    --flame-halo: rgba(255, 140, 60, 0.45);
  }

  .curiosity-trigger:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid var(--accent);
    outline-offset: 4px;
  }

  .curiosity-trigger:active {
    transform: translateY(1px) scale(0.97);
  }

  .curiosity-flame {
    filter: drop-shadow(0 0 0.08em var(--flame-halo));
    transition: filter 0.3s ease;
  }

  .curiosity-trigger:hover .curiosity-flame,
  .curiosity-trigger:focus-visible .curiosity-flame {
    filter: drop-shadow(0 0 0.06em var(--flame-halo)) drop-shadow(0 0 0.22em var(--flame-halo));
  }

  .curiosity-letter {
    display: inline-block;
    /* Each letter carries its own copy of the gradient, shifted by its index, so the band
       still reads as one sweep while the letters move independently. */
    background: linear-gradient(
      100deg,
      var(--flame-ember) 0%,
      var(--flame-heat) 22%,
      var(--flame-glow) 40%,
      var(--flame-core) 50%,
      var(--flame-glow) 60%,
      var(--flame-heat) 78%,
      var(--flame-ember) 100%
    );
    background-size: 900% 100%;
    background-clip: text;
    -webkit-background-clip: text;
    color: transparent;
    -webkit-text-fill-color: transparent;
    transition: transform 0.3s cubic-bezier(0.34, 1.56, 0.64, 1) calc(var(--i) * 25ms);
    animation:
      curiosity-burn 3.2s linear calc(var(--i) * 0.11s - 3.2s) infinite,
      curiosity-wave 7s ease-in-out calc(var(--i) * 70ms) infinite;
  }

  .curiosity-trigger:hover .curiosity-letter,
  .curiosity-trigger:focus-visible .curiosity-letter {
    animation: curiosity-burn 3.2s linear calc(var(--i) * 0.11s - 3.2s) infinite;
    transform: translateY(-0.07em);
  }

  @keyframes curiosity-burn {
    from {
      background-position: 100% 0;
    }
    to {
      background-position: 0% 0;
    }
  }

  @keyframes curiosity-wave {
    0%,
    14%,
    100% {
      transform: translateY(0);
    }
    5% {
      transform: translateY(-0.14em);
    }
    9% {
      transform: translateY(0.02em);
    }
  }

  .curiosity-trigger[aria-expanded='true'] .curiosity-flame {
    filter: none;
  }

  .curiosity-trigger[aria-expanded='true'] .curiosity-letter {
    animation: none;
    transform: none;
    background: none;
    color: var(--ink);
    -webkit-text-fill-color: currentColor;
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .curiosity-trigger,
    .curiosity-letter,
    .curiosity-flame {
      transition: none;
    }

    .curiosity-letter,
    .curiosity-trigger:hover .curiosity-letter,
    .curiosity-trigger:focus-visible .curiosity-letter {
      animation: none;
      transform: none;
      background-position: 50% 0;
    }

    .curiosity-trigger:active {
      transform: none;
    }
  }
</style>
</BaseLayout>
